<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore new service apartment supply to triple.</title>
<headline>Singapore new service apartment supply to triple.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Developers will add 1,019 service apartments in Singapore this year, three times the number of new ones in 1996, real estate consultant Richard Ellis said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The new units will bring the total number of service apartments in Singapore to 3,015 in 1997. Anther 391 units are expected to come on stream by 1999.</p>
<p>The service apartment sector is dominated by property tycoon Ng Teng Fong's Far East Organisation which has 28 percent of the market or 568 units.  </p>
<p>New operators this year include Fraser &amp; Neave Ltd, Shangri-La Hotel Ltd, United Engineers Ltd and Wing Tai Holdings Ltd, Richard Ellis said in a statement.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
